From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:04:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 100/108] test(e2e): encrypted backup by the GUI/service
 writer, read back by our readers and the official client

The suite only ran the CLIs: the writer the GUI and the service use
(RunBackupInline / ChunkState) never met a real PBS, which let it index
encrypted chunks under the bare sha256 (issue #13), and no GUI read path
(catalog, search, restore) ever read an encrypted directory backup.

Test 11 runs gui/e2e_live_test.go (skipped outside the suite) against the
suite's PBS: an encrypted backup with RunBackupInline and the official
client's key file; the catalog read directly (ListSnapshotContents' silent
fallback to the data archive hid the #13 failure); a search; a restore
compared byte for byte with the source; the same restore refused without
the key; and test 1's unencrypted snapshot restored with the key loaded.
The official client then restores the GUI snapshot identically (minus the
GUI's metadata file) and refuses it without the key.

The e2e job installs the GUI test libraries; the new file is gofmt-checked.
